{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "CPC1008NTR",
 "kind": "relay",
 "manufacturer": "IXYS Integrated Circuits Division (Littelfuse)",
 "title": "Single-pole normally open (1-Form-A) OptoMOS solid-state relay, 100 V, 150 mA, 4-pin SOP",
 "source": {
  "revision": "DS-CPC1008N-R11, 5/25/2017",
  "pages": 6
 },
 "summary": "The CPC1008N is a tiny 1-Form-A solid-state relay: light from an input LED, coupled across an isolation barrier, turns on a pair of MOSFETs that form the normally open output. It blocks 100 V peak, carries 150 mA AC or DC with no more than 8 Ω on-resistance, and isolates input from output to 1500 Vrms. The output has no contacts, so it switches without arcing or EMI and needs no snubber. It is halogen-free and rated UL 94 V-0.",
